# 5. P0 — REMOVE DUPLICATE SCHOOL REVIEW COMPLETION

The School dossier currently displays two primary controls for completing the same review:

- "Hoàn tất xét sơ hồ sơ".
- "Hoàn tất xét sơ".

This is unacceptable.

## Required change

Keep exactly ONE primary authorized completion action.

Preferred label:

**"Hoàn tất xét sơ tuyển"**

Place it at the natural completion point of the dossier.

Remove other duplicate completion buttons.

Do not create a floating duplicate elsewhere.

## Verify canonical semantics

Before allowing completion, check the actual approved rules.

Manual criterion conclusions must remain authoritative.

Do not assume evidence-review counts alone establish a criterion conclusion.

A criterion can be:

- Unreviewed.
- Partially assessed.
- Explicitly concluded Pass.
- Explicitly concluded Fail.

The system may have:

- Five criteria conclusively reviewed.
- Four Pass.
- One Fail.

This is a completed human review even though it does not meet all five criteria.

## Completion feedback

After confirmed server success:

Show one clear compact status:

**"Đã hoàn tất xét sơ tuyển"**

Use a check icon and relevant timestamp if available.

Replace or disable the original completion action according to the actual lifecycle.

Do not show another large success dialog unnecessarily.

Do not automatically include the Student in the official School forwarding list.

School final forwarding remains a separate intentional selection-and-PDF action.

## Failure

If the server rejects completion, do not show the success state.

Show the relevant blocking reason or missing human conclusions.

